# Research : UV trim sheet, texel density, stacking, packing (19 October 2026)

Notes of the web research done for ZenRay UV Trimsheet, kept on disk so that nothing is lost. Each line : what the source says, what we take from it. (19 October 2026)

| Topic | Source | What we keep | Date |
|---|---|---|---|
| Trim layout plus normal structure, UV mapping script | GDC 2015 talk The Ultimate Trim, Sunset Overdrive (Insomniac), talk link not verified ; [polycount thread reproducing it](https://polycount.com/discussion/comment/2793276) | trims work cleanly with 90 degree hard edges ; a UV border must not straddle two normal directions ; a script lays out UVs at equal texel density | 19 October 2026 |
| Texel density per camera | [Maxon, Texel Density](https://help.maxon.net/c4d/en-us/Content/html/Texel_Density.html), [polycount](https://polycount.com/discussion/comment/2702528), [StraySpark guide](https://www.strayspark.studio/blog/texture-resolution-guide-games-512-1k-2k-4k) | 10.24 px/cm (1024 px/m) first person, 5.12 px/cm (512 px/m) third person, 2.56 px/cm top down ; 2048 px/m for hero close ups | 19 October 2026 |
| Consistent density over per asset priority | [polycount, UDIMs](https://polycount.com/discussion/183032/udims), [polycount comment](https://polycount.com/discussion/comment/2709190) | one density everywhere ; trims stay at the correct density | 19 October 2026 |
| UDIM versus second material | [polycount, UDIMs](https://polycount.com/discussion/comment/2593030), [UDIM guide](https://www.seeles.ai/features/tools/dcc-udim-texture-workflow-guide) | UDIM costs memory and draw calls in real time ; splitting into a second material, or a non square sheet (2048 x 4096), is the usual game answer | 19 October 2026 |
| Padding and gutter | [polycount, padding](https://polycount.com/discussion/191707/padding), [Adobe, dilation](https://experienceleague.adobe.com/en/docs/substance-3d-painter/using/technical-support/workflow-issues/export-issues/texture-dilation-or-padding), [gamedev.net](https://gamedev.net/forums/topic/685357-uv-padding/) | padding is the bleed of each island, the gap is about twice it ; 4 to 8 px at 2048 with anisotropic filtering, 16 px conservative ; islands snapped to the pixel grid | 19 October 2026 |
| Mirrored UVs and tangent space | [MikkTSpace header](https://projects.blender.org/archive/blender-archive/raw/commit/c7cfee04c4dd9dcafebe1659d7f7cf1ffd7ff14e/intern/mikktspace/mikktspace.h), [Blender issue 53750](https://projects.blender.org/blender/blender/issues/53750), [PlayCanvas forum](https://forum.playcanvas.com/t/issue-with-mirrored-normal-map/41745) | the bitangent sign follows UV handedness ; mirrored islands work with MikkTSpace but a mirror seam is a real seam ; a proper (rotation) stack keeps handedness | 19 October 2026 |
| Stacking identical islands | [SideFX UV Layout 3.0 HDK header](https://sidefx.com/docs/hdk/_s_o_p___u_v_layout-3_80_8h_source.html), [UV Stacker](https://sidefx.com/tutorials/h16-game-shelf-tools-uv-stacker/), [forum bug 156601](https://www.sidefx.com/forum/post/428744) | UV Layout stacks by area with a 0.02 length tolerance and can stack mirrored ; it guesses by area, so we prove congruence by a rigid fit instead | 19 October 2026 |
| Rectangle packing | [Jylanki, A Thousand Ways to Pack the Bin](https://gorillasun.de/blog/rectangle-packing-an-incredibly-difficult-problem), [rectpack](https://gitee.com/silent790/rectpack) | Shelf, Skyline, MaxRects, Guillotine heuristics ; a band of a trim sheet IS a shelf : height fixed by the tallest island, filled left to right | 19 October 2026 |
| Chart segmentation and packing pipeline | [xatlas](https://github.com/jpcy/xatlas) | segment charts, parameterize, pack, in separate stages that can be re run | 19 October 2026 |
| Trim mapping tools | Trim Mapper (Blender), Propgon UV Trim (Quadrify), SideFX Labs Trim Texture | straighten quad strips from topology, orient, stack ; Labs tool lacks documentation and fitting control | 19 October 2026 |
| Straighten grid UVs in Houdini | [UV Flatten cut sew align straighten](https://sidefx.com/tutorials/uv-flatten-cut-sew-align-straighten/), [forum topic 100829](https://www.sidefx.com/forum/topic/100829/?page=1) | UV Flatten aligns in U or V and straightens edge loops ; studios straighten a strip then set its length by script | 19 October 2026 |
| Rasterize UVs in Copernicus | [Rasterize Geometry COP](https://www.sidefx.com/ja/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/rasterizegeo.html), [Labs UV Grid Texture](https://80.lv/articles/new-copernicus-node-for-testing-uv-layouts-on-3d-models) | Rasterize Setup in UV space plus Rasterize Geometry draws the layout from a SOP import ; polygons only, no packed | 19 October 2026 |
